From 9aa9b2592b84b363ccef7dd884737870c939d8ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sbihaiko <bihaiko@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:42:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] video_core: count-only counters for the split's back
 (EDEN_NX2_COUNTERS)

Profile zones read the clock twice each, ~2.6 million times a second on the
back, which costs it an estimated 135 ms a second and skews what they measure.
EDEN_NX2_COUNTERS=1 counts without reading the clock, and logs every 10 s:

- Fast draw break sets: for each draw that lost its delta chain to a state
  change, the distinct breaks made on the back since the previous draw, not
  only the last. The log gives set sizes, sole breaks, pairs, breaks by draw,
  and the draws broken only by EDEN_NX2_FAST_DRAW_PROBE methods (default
  0x54c clear_report_value, 0x556 render_enable mode), the draws a change to
  those methods would turn into delta draws.
- The back's ring entries by kind (direct, run and sunk methods, multi,
  register blocks, constant buffer data, calls), and its deferred calls by
  thunk address, with an anchor address to look them up in the symbols ELF.
- The executable 3D methods the back runs, by method, with their share of
  same-value writes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
